  "body": "Follow-up of #1953 (item 2: behaviour tests do not depend on the look).\n\nThe ribbon cells are painted, not widgets. They have no AccessKit node. So about 35 behaviour tests click a ribbon cell at `cell.rect.center()` from the plan geometry: `mill_plan_at(1280.0)`, `panes::view_rows_of`, `recent_drop::rows_of`, `theme_drop::rows_of`. These tests break when a refit moves or resizes the ribbon, but the behaviour did not change.\n\nTests that use this geometry (inventory comment on #1953):\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`: 13 tests (for example `post_cell_queues_and_the_file_arm_runs_the_gate`, `ribbon_drill_cell_creates_a_drill_operation`, `simulate_cell_arms_transport_and_stop_disarms`)\n- `tests/first_setup.rs`, `tests/layout.rs` (4), `tests/recent_door.rs` (7), `tests/theme_door.rs` (2), `tests/setup_picks_disarm.rs` (2), `tests/machines_pane.rs` / `tests/machines_edit.rs` (through `open_machines`)\n\nWhat to do:\n1. Give each painted ribbon cell, and each row of its drop lists (View, Recent, Theme, section drops), an AccessKit node with its label and role (`Button`, `MenuItem`).\n2. Change the tests to click the node by label (`get_by_label(..).click()`).\n3. Keep the plan-only tests (`every_kind_has_a_home_on_every_machine`, `every_section_lives_behind_its_door_at_every_width`). They are layout tests by design.\n\nDone means: no behaviour test computes a ribbon cell position, and the `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` does not go down.\n",
